{
  "id": "21485_furikakeru",
  "headword": "{振|ふ}りかける",
  "reading": "ふりかける",
  "romaji": "furikakeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to sprinkle over; to scatter on top of",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to sprinkle over; to scatter on top of",
      "explanation": "To scatter a dry or fine-grained substance such as salt, spices, or sesame seeds onto the surface of food or another object."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21485_furikakeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "ご{飯|はん}にふりかけを{振|ふ}りかける。",
      "english": "To sprinkle furikake on rice.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21485_furikakeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "サラダに{塩|しお}とコショウを{振|ふ}りかけた。",
      "english": "I sprinkled salt and pepper on the salad.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21485_furikakeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{仕上|しあ}げに{粉|こな}チーズをたっぷり{振|ふ}りかけると、{風味|ふうみ}がぐっと{増|ま}す。",
      "english": "Sprinkling plenty of grated cheese on top as a finishing touch greatly enhances the flavor.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb from {振|ふ}る (to shake, scatter) + かける (to apply onto), meaning to sprinkle or scatter something onto a surface. Most commonly used in cooking contexts.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Almost always used for dry or fine ingredients (salt, pepper, spices, cheese, sesame seeds)\n- The noun ふりかけ (rice seasoning) derives from this verb\n- Can also be used figuratively, e.g., {水|みず}を{振|ふ}りかける (to sprinkle water)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {塩|しお}を{振|ふ}りかける: to sprinkle salt\n- ごまを{振|ふ}りかける: to sprinkle sesame seeds\n- {粉|こな}チーズを{振|ふ}りかける: to sprinkle grated cheese\n- パセリを{振|ふ}りかける: to sprinkle parsley\n- {水|みず}を{振|ふ}りかける: to sprinkle water\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- まぶす: to coat evenly; implies covering the entire surface\n- {散|ち}らす: to scatter; broader meaning, not limited to cooking\n- かける: to pour over; used for liquids rather than dry ingredients",
